  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A rectangular region is bounded by the graphs of the equations \\(y=a,\\) \\(y=-b,\\) \\(x=-c,\\) and \\(x=d,\\) where \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c,\\) and \\(d\\) are all positive numbers. Which of the following represents the area of this region?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(ac+ad+bc+bd\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(ac-ad+bc-bd\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(ac+ad-bc-bd\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-ac-ad+bc+bd\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(ac-ad-bc+bd\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2011-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Note that the region is a rectangle with side lengths \\[ a - (-b) = a + b \\] and \\[ d - (-c) = c + d. \\] The area is then \\[ (a + b)(c + d) =\\]\\[ ac + ad + bc + bd. \\]\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Find the vertical and horizontal side lengths of the rectangle",
        "The side lengths are \\(a+b\\) and \\(c+d\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
